<h2>Local or cloud</h2>
<p>Local profiles play offline and on private servers. Public servers require a cloud account with a unique username, email and password. Account names identify your public match results across servers; avatars, favorite tanks and controls remain settings on each device.</p>
<h2>Sign in on a client</h2>
<p>On macOS, Windows or Linux, choose <strong>Cloud profile</strong> in the profile picker and sign in with your username and password. You can create an account from the same window. On AmigaOS, choose <strong>Profile type → Cloud</strong> when creating or editing a profile.</p>
<p>Usernames contain 3–15 letters, numbers or underscores and start with a letter. Passwords contain 12–72 bytes. Clients remember a login session, never the password. When a session expires, sign in again through Cloud profile. Each player needs their own account.</p>
<h2>Connect Apple TV</h2>
<p>Choose <strong>Cloud profile</strong> on Apple TV. On your phone or computer, open <a href="/account/pin">openfp.retrocs.org/account/pin</a>, enter the displayed PIN and sign in. PINs expire after ten minutes and can be used once. Other clients use username and password directly.</p>
<h2>Password recovery</h2>
<p><a href="/account/">Manage sign-in and recovery</a> on the website. Password recovery is available only when the site administrator has configured SMTP. A used recovery link signs out existing client sessions. Deleting a device's local profile does not delete the central account.</p>
<h2>For operators</h2>
<p>Update the website database with <code>php inc/migrate.php up</code>. Public servers need a registration generated by <code>php inc/cloud-server.php my-server</code>. Add the printed hash to the website's private <code>accounts.servers</code> configuration and the credentials to the dedicated server configuration. Private servers (<code>public = no</code>) need no registration. Join-code servers accept local profiles but need registration for the listing service.</p>
<p>The optional <code>smtp</code> configuration supports a relay hostname/IP, port, STARTTLS, implicit TLS or no encryption, optional authentication, sender address, EHLO hostname and source IP binding. Recovery is automatically disabled if no relay and sender are configured.</p>
<p><code>php inc/reset-data.php</code> previews a full user-data reset. The explicit <code>--confirm ERASE-ALL-USER-DATA</code> option deletes accounts, statistics, match history and community uploads. Back up the database and stop writers first. Configuration, schema and built-in maps remain.</p>
<p>See the <a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/openfp/blob/main/docs/ACCOUNTS.md">complete operator guide</a> for setup, SMTP fields, protocol compatibility and reset details.</p>
